The five logo marks are taken from microsoft/fluentui-emoji at commit
62ecdc0d7ca5c6df32148c169556bc8d3782fca4, in the Color style, which is the
design Windows 11 renders:

- emoji-cherry-blossom.svg
  https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji/blob/62ecdc0d7ca5c6df32148c169556bc8d3782fca4/assets/Cherry%20blossom/Color/cherry_blossom_color.svg
- emoji-blossom.svg
  https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji/blob/62ecdc0d7ca5c6df32148c169556bc8d3782fca4/assets/Blossom/Color/blossom_color.svg
- emoji-hibiscus.svg
  https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji/blob/62ecdc0d7ca5c6df32148c169556bc8d3782fca4/assets/Hibiscus/Color/hibiscus_color.svg
- emoji-snowflake.svg
  https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji/blob/62ecdc0d7ca5c6df32148c169556bc8d3782fca4/assets/Snowflake/Color/snowflake_color.svg
- emoji-broccoli.svg
  https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji/blob/62ecdc0d7ca5c6df32148c169556bc8d3782fca4/assets/Broccoli/Color/broccoli_color.svg

Each is passed through svgo 4.0.2 with --precision=2 --multipass, which halves
the byte count and changes no drawn shape. The artwork is otherwise verbatim.

