codex.svg comes from the same project at a later commit, because the Codex mark
did not exist at the one above:

- codex.svg
  https://github.com/lobehub/lobe-icons/blob/63c800e3db6427b3f156f7b88d426ccb3f7277a1/packages/static-svg/icons/codex-color.svg

codex.svg drops the white app-icon plate and tightens the viewBox to the glyph,
so it renders at the same optical size as the other provider marks.

microsoft-color.svg is the four-square Microsoft logo, which upstream files
under the Azure name; its title is changed to "Microsoft".

lobe-icons ships Jina as one `currentColor` path and no colour variant.
jina-color.svg splits that path at its two subpaths — the dot and the J — and
fills them with Jina's own brand colours, sampled as the two dominant opaque
values of the 256x256 mark at https://jina.ai/favicon.ico: #EB6161 for the dot
and #009191 for the J.

Everything else here is verbatim: take a replacement from the static-svg
directory above rather than from a rendered page, whose gradient ids carry
React's per-render suffix.

